1
00:00:09,187 --> 00:00:11,187
[water rushing]

2
00:00:14,229 --> 00:00:15,979
[woodpecker drilling]

3
00:00:52,437 --> 00:00:53,479
[snarling]

4
00:00:55,896 --> 00:00:57,021
[screeching]

5
00:00:58,604 --> 00:01:00,062
-[yells]
-[screeches]

6
00:01:04,479 --> 00:01:05,687
[grunting]

7
00:01:09,396 --> 00:01:10,896
[growls]

8
00:01:10,979 --> 00:01:12,104
[hisses]

9
00:01:18,062 --> 00:01:19,354
[neighs]

10
00:01:39,854 --> 00:01:41,521
[screeches]

11
00:01:52,937 --> 00:01:54,271
[sighs]

12
00:02:05,021 --> 00:02:06,521
Today isn't your day, is it?

13
00:02:10,979 --> 00:02:12,479
[sniffs]

14
00:02:14,812 --> 00:02:16,354
-[grunts]
-[sword slashes]

15
00:02:40,687 --> 00:02:42,687
[lively buzz of conversation]

16
00:02:47,604 --> 00:02:49,062
[fiddle playing]

17
00:02:52,604 --> 00:02:54,104
-[shushing]
-[music stops]

18
00:02:54,187 --> 00:02:56,187
[scattered whispers]

19
00:03:00,604 --> 00:03:01,646
What will it be?

20
00:03:02,687 --> 00:03:04,354
Point me to the alderman's house.

21
00:03:04,437 --> 00:03:06,854
-It's down the alley to the left--
-Isadora.

22
00:03:13,771 --> 00:03:15,687
We don't want your kind here, Witcher.

23
00:03:16,687 --> 00:03:17,687
The alderman,

24
00:03:18,396 --> 00:03:20,812
tell me where he is
and I'll be on my way.

25
00:03:21,979 --> 00:03:23,937
You don't give the orders around here...

26
00:03:24,021 --> 00:03:26,354
[scoffs] you mutant son of a bitch.

27
00:03:26,854 --> 00:03:28,187
[low thump]

28
00:03:29,229 --> 00:03:31,312
-[innkeeper] Hear that?
-[low rumble]

29
00:03:31,396 --> 00:03:32,396
Go.

30
00:03:32,479 --> 00:03:35,437
On your own or at the end of a rope,
your choice.

31
00:03:36,854 --> 00:03:37,896
Not a hard choice.

32
00:03:38,271 --> 00:03:40,646
Yeah, fuck that. Kill him
with your bare hands if you have to.

33
00:03:43,104 --> 00:03:45,479
C'mon, Witcher.
You're not scared of us, are ya?

34
00:03:48,521 --> 00:03:51,521
-Show us what you've got.
-Can you not leave it alone for a moment?

35
00:03:58,312 --> 00:04:01,104
-Witchers can't be trusted.
-[woman] I'm not speaking to you.

36
00:04:03,104 --> 00:04:05,854
I apologize
for my man's interference in your day.

37
00:04:08,312 --> 00:04:11,521
Hopefully he can improve his behavior
by tomorrow's market.

38
00:04:13,771 --> 00:04:15,062
Sorry, Renfri.

39
00:04:18,312 --> 00:04:19,521
Come on, lads.

40
00:04:21,687 --> 00:04:23,687
Beer for my friend here and one for me.

41
00:04:23,771 --> 00:04:24,979
[fiddle resumes playing]

42
00:04:25,062 --> 00:04:25,937
[snorts]

43
00:04:27,896 --> 00:04:30,146
I am speaking to you now, good sir.

44
00:04:31,354 --> 00:04:33,354
[lively conversation resumes]

45
00:04:43,562 --> 00:04:44,687
Want some breakfast?

46
00:04:46,854 --> 00:04:47,854
I'm full.

47
00:04:49,771 --> 00:04:50,646
Venison.

48
00:05:09,229 --> 00:05:10,354
[sighs]

49
00:05:13,854 --> 00:05:16,229
My mother, God rest her,
would be mortified.

50
00:05:17,854 --> 00:05:19,062
Our secret, then.

51
00:05:28,229 --> 00:05:30,396
So, what brings you to Blaviken,
White Hair?

52
00:05:30,854 --> 00:05:32,187
You came for a monster?

53
00:05:33,146 --> 00:05:34,687
I was traveling by the swamp.

54
00:05:34,771 --> 00:05:38,062
That would be your mistake, then.
Why wouldn't you travel by main roads?

55
00:05:39,646 --> 00:05:41,354
It's hard to make a living on main roads.

56
00:05:42,229 --> 00:05:44,562
And you desperately need money
for new clothes.

57
00:05:50,271 --> 00:05:51,271
Two more beers.

58
00:06:06,771 --> 00:06:08,104
[sighs]

59
00:06:08,187 --> 00:06:10,729
More and more,
I find monsters wherever I go.

60
00:06:23,854 --> 00:06:25,771
How much coin for your kikimora, then?

61
00:06:40,104 --> 00:06:42,271
I killed a rat this morning
with my breakfast fork.

62
00:06:42,979 --> 00:06:44,979
Stabbed it in its fat little gut.

63
00:06:45,562 --> 00:06:47,771
My mother nearly fainted,
but what was I supposed to do?

64
00:06:47,854 --> 00:06:50,021
It had been shitting in our pantry
for days.

65
00:06:54,812 --> 00:06:57,021
-[Witcher] You mentioned coin.
-[girl] Yes.

66
00:06:57,521 --> 00:06:59,687
Isadora said you were looking
for my father.

67
00:07:00,187 --> 00:07:01,771
She's a gossip, you see.

68
00:07:01,854 --> 00:07:03,812
Probably went two steps
into the Lord's Inn

69
00:07:03,896 --> 00:07:07,104
before she was running off telling
everyone an evil witcher had arrived.

70
00:07:07,187 --> 00:07:08,021
[horse snorts]

71
00:07:10,062 --> 00:07:11,104
You don't scare me.

72
00:07:11,812 --> 00:07:12,979
That's too bad.

73
00:07:13,062 --> 00:07:15,146
And I can also tell you

74
00:07:15,812 --> 00:07:17,979
that my father will have no use
for this beast.

75
00:07:18,062 --> 00:07:19,021
Your father,

76
00:07:19,729 --> 00:07:20,729
the alderman?

77
00:07:21,937 --> 00:07:23,271
He posted a flyer.

78
00:07:24,354 --> 00:07:25,396
For a graveir.

79
00:07:26,021 --> 00:07:27,312
kikimoras are useful.

80
00:07:28,479 --> 00:07:29,729
Population control.

81
00:07:31,646 --> 00:07:32,854
Hm.

82
00:07:33,687 --> 00:07:35,521
You should speak to Master Irion,
our wizard.

83
00:07:36,979 --> 00:07:39,896
He's willing to pay for odds and ends
he needs for elixirs.

84
00:07:41,021 --> 00:07:42,646
I sold him our dog when it died.

85
00:07:43,479 --> 00:07:44,396
Mysteriously.

86
00:07:47,521 --> 00:07:48,354
Fine.

87
00:07:48,979 --> 00:07:50,104
Take me to him.

88
00:07:51,646 --> 00:07:54,021
I got 15 crowns for the yappy mutt.

89
00:07:55,854 --> 00:07:59,229
That's enough to buy some new clothes.
Just saying.

90
00:08:01,062 --> 00:08:02,146
Hm.

91
00:08:02,229 --> 00:08:03,354
Come on, Roach.

92
00:08:03,896 --> 00:08:05,229
[whinnies]

93
00:08:08,146 --> 00:08:10,062
[girl] Have you ever killed a succubus?

94
00:08:10,396 --> 00:08:11,687
A striga?

95
00:08:12,604 --> 00:08:13,646
Werewolf?

96
00:08:14,312 --> 00:08:15,729
She-wolf?

97
00:08:15,812 --> 00:08:16,979
That's not a thing.

98
00:08:17,646 --> 00:08:19,062
So you've killed the rest?

99
00:08:19,604 --> 00:08:21,104
I think that makes you a hero.

100
00:08:22,271 --> 00:08:25,187
My mother says
you're the offspring of foul sorcery,

101
00:08:25,271 --> 00:08:28,687
a diabolic creation,
a filthy degenerate born of Hell.

102
00:08:29,812 --> 00:08:31,271
Have you ever been to Hell?

103
00:08:32,354 --> 00:08:33,896
I've never even left Blaviken.

104
00:08:33,979 --> 00:08:35,562
Because my mother's never left Blaviken,

105
00:08:35,646 --> 00:08:39,021
and if it's good enough for Libushe,
then it's good enough for Marilka.

106
00:08:39,104 --> 00:08:40,687
-That's my name.
-[goat bleats]

107
00:08:40,771 --> 00:08:41,646
Marilka.

108
00:08:42,687 --> 00:08:43,687
Like milk.

109
00:08:45,229 --> 00:08:46,229
What's your name?

110
00:08:47,229 --> 00:08:48,229
Geralt.

111
00:08:49,271 --> 00:08:50,354
Like garroter?

112
00:08:51,354 --> 00:08:52,354
Nice.

113
00:08:53,021 --> 00:08:54,396
Where are you from, Geralt?

114
00:08:55,229 --> 00:08:56,271
Rivia.

115
00:08:58,146 --> 00:09:01,729
I don't know where that is,
but I could learn, if you'd let me.

116
00:09:02,312 --> 00:09:03,271
No.

117
00:09:04,646 --> 00:09:07,396
Because I'm a girl
and girls can't be witchers.

118
00:09:07,854 --> 00:09:10,271
Which I think is probably
the stupidest thing I've ever heard.

119
00:09:10,354 --> 00:09:11,271
Hm.

120
00:09:12,104 --> 00:09:13,062
I want more.

121
00:09:14,104 --> 00:09:15,104
I have to be more,

122
00:09:15,187 --> 00:09:17,812
because I don't know what to do
in Blaviken for the rest of my life,

123
00:09:17,896 --> 00:09:19,646
except go to the boring old market.

124
00:09:20,521 --> 00:09:21,562
And kill rats.

125
00:09:22,062 --> 00:09:23,104
And dogs.

126
00:09:28,604 --> 00:09:29,729
Here we are.

127
00:09:36,729 --> 00:09:37,812
Hold Roach.

128
00:09:38,521 --> 00:09:40,104
-[whinnies]
-Be nice.

129
00:09:41,687 --> 00:09:42,771
[Marilka] Hey, Roach.

130
00:09:50,979 --> 00:09:52,562
[chiming sound]

131
00:09:52,646 --> 00:09:54,312
[low, resonating hum]

132
00:10:10,396 --> 00:10:12,229
[bird calling]

133
00:10:21,437 --> 00:10:22,396
Greetings.

134
00:10:23,687 --> 00:10:24,812
I am Stregobor.

135
00:10:27,479 --> 00:10:29,312
Master Stregobor.

136
00:10:30,187 --> 00:10:31,062
Sorcerer.

137
00:10:31,146 --> 00:10:33,271
I have a kikimora for Master Irion.

138
00:10:33,354 --> 00:10:35,729
Yes, well, forgive the confusion.

139
00:10:35,812 --> 00:10:39,479
Irion created this tower,
but he's been dead 200 years.

140
00:10:40,437 --> 00:10:43,646
So, in order to honor him,
I've taken his name as my...

141
00:10:44,354 --> 00:10:46,437
personal sobriquet.

142
00:10:46,937 --> 00:10:48,104
Hm.

143
00:10:48,187 --> 00:10:49,812
He create this illusion, too?

144
00:10:49,896 --> 00:10:51,562
No, this is, uh... this is...

145
00:10:52,562 --> 00:10:54,062
my own creation.

146
00:10:55,479 --> 00:10:57,271
Helps pass time more delightfully.

147
00:10:58,021 --> 00:11:00,687
Because you're in hiding, Stregobor.

148
00:11:00,771 --> 00:11:02,229
How very clever of you...

149
00:11:03,479 --> 00:11:04,479
Witcher.

150
00:11:12,521 --> 00:11:15,021
Not often do we see your likeness
here in Blaviken.

151
00:11:15,104 --> 00:11:16,812
Not many of my likeness left.

152
00:11:17,354 --> 00:11:18,312
Hm.

153
00:11:19,021 --> 00:11:21,812
I'd offer you my condolences, but...

154
00:11:22,646 --> 00:11:24,979
I seem to remember
that witchers don't feel...

155
00:11:25,896 --> 00:11:26,896
anything.

156
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:30,729
I'm grateful destiny brought you to me.

157
00:11:30,812 --> 00:11:32,021
Marilka brought me to you.

158
00:11:32,104 --> 00:11:34,437
Oh, Marilka. Marilka works for me.

159
00:11:35,979 --> 00:11:36,979
Now and then.

160
00:11:38,229 --> 00:11:39,979
On matters of great import.

161
00:11:40,854 --> 00:11:43,312
A reclusive sorcerer who uses an alias

162
00:11:43,396 --> 00:11:46,104
and hires a young girl
to procure him a witcher.

163
00:11:47,021 --> 00:11:48,354
You don't want my monster.

164
00:11:49,812 --> 00:11:51,354
You want me to kill yours.

165
00:11:51,437 --> 00:11:52,437
Very clever.

166
00:11:53,354 --> 00:11:54,187
Indeed.

167
00:11:54,271 --> 00:11:56,104
-What kind?
-The worst kind.

168
00:11:58,104 --> 00:11:59,187
The human kind.

169
00:12:00,604 --> 00:12:01,979
Its name is Renfri.

170
00:12:05,312 --> 00:12:06,521
Hm.

171
00:12:16,229 --> 00:12:17,229
-[laughter]
-Damn it.

172
00:12:18,104 --> 00:12:19,437
-[sighs]
-Go on, Martin.

173
00:12:20,187 --> 00:12:21,479
-Ah! Five.
-Yeah!

174
00:12:22,271 --> 00:12:24,562
-Not yet.
-There's no way you can get five.

175
00:12:24,646 --> 00:12:26,812
You're not taking a bite of that bread
before I try.

176
00:12:26,896 --> 00:12:28,479
[distant clatter of hooves]

177
00:12:35,979 --> 00:12:38,187
-Better throw those knuckles.
-Go on, then.

178
00:12:38,271 --> 00:12:39,771
[hoofbeats approaching]

179
00:12:39,854 --> 00:12:41,229
-[laughter]
-Told ya.

180
00:12:44,146 --> 00:12:45,854
I didn't steal the bread. Korin did!

181
00:12:45,937 --> 00:12:47,937
-Quick! Quick!
-Hey, shut up, you twat!

182
00:12:50,021 --> 00:12:51,562
You need to come with us.

183
00:12:56,854 --> 00:13:00,062
[woman] As your Queen,
I grant you this commendation,

184
00:13:00,646 --> 00:13:04,146
which will symbolize your duty
and bond as liegemen

185
00:13:04,229 --> 00:13:06,729
in fealty to the crown of Cintra.

186
00:13:13,021 --> 00:13:16,312
Could use with a bit of feel-ty myself
right now.

187
00:13:20,229 --> 00:13:21,062
Gross.

188
00:13:21,146 --> 00:13:24,687
[Queen] Do you promise to defend
to your utmost the weak, the orphaned...

189
00:13:24,771 --> 00:13:28,437
-Late wee pups don't get to bark.
-I was playing in the square.

190
00:13:28,521 --> 00:13:29,646
...speak only the truth...

191
00:13:29,729 --> 00:13:31,937
-Knucklebones?
-...loyal and brave...

192
00:13:32,021 --> 00:13:33,979
Did you win this time?
Like I showed you.

193
00:13:34,062 --> 00:13:35,729
-...at any cost...
-I would have,

194
00:13:35,812 --> 00:13:38,312
if the horsemen of doom hadn't
ridden up like that.

195
00:13:38,396 --> 00:13:40,854
-I grant you this...
-If you can't win a game of knucklebones

196
00:13:40,937 --> 00:13:42,812
-for fear of a few horses...
-...duty and bond...

197
00:13:42,896 --> 00:13:44,562
...what'll you do when you go into battle?

198
00:13:44,646 --> 00:13:47,146
-...in fealty to the crown of Cintra.
-[sighs]

199
00:13:47,229 --> 00:13:49,479
[sighs]
At least you didn't shit your kecks.

200
00:13:51,521 --> 00:13:52,812
As members of the Royal Family,

201
00:13:52,896 --> 00:13:57,187
is it too much to ask
that you exercise a modicum of respect?

202
00:13:58,479 --> 00:13:59,562
Especially you.

203
00:14:00,854 --> 00:14:03,979
This is your duty
as king and grandfather.

204
00:14:05,521 --> 00:14:06,354
[King sighs]

205
00:14:06,437 --> 00:14:09,437
Grant me leave, my Queen.
I am worn from my trip to the Isles.

206
00:14:11,729 --> 00:14:13,937
And my bedchamber duties before that.

207
00:14:14,729 --> 00:14:15,604
Gross.

208
00:14:16,646 --> 00:14:17,771
-[chuckles]
-As your Queen,

209
00:14:17,854 --> 00:14:20,312
I grant you this commendation,

210
00:14:20,396 --> 00:14:22,771
which will symbolize
your duty and bond...

211
00:14:22,854 --> 00:14:26,146
[Stregobor]
Destiny has many faces, Witcher.

212
00:14:26,937 --> 00:14:29,437
Mine, for example,
is beautiful on the outside, but...

213
00:14:30,021 --> 00:14:31,271
hideous on the inside.

214
00:14:31,937 --> 00:14:34,854
She has stretched her bloody talons
towards me.

215
00:14:34,937 --> 00:14:36,271
Wizards are all the same.

216
00:14:36,896 --> 00:14:40,062
You talk nonsense
while making wise and meaningful faces.

217
00:14:42,062 --> 00:14:44,187
Speak normally.

218
00:14:48,271 --> 00:14:49,729
Have you ever heard of the...

219
00:14:50,562 --> 00:14:51,937
Curse of the Black Sun?

220
00:14:53,146 --> 00:14:56,062
First full eclipse in 1,200 years.

221
00:14:56,146 --> 00:14:58,146
It marked the imminent return
of Lilit,

222
00:14:59,146 --> 00:15:02,979
demon goddess of the night
sent to exterminate the human race.

223
00:15:04,062 --> 00:15:06,021
According to the wise mage Eltibald,

224
00:15:07,021 --> 00:15:11,146
Lilit's path was to be prepared
by 60 women wearing gold crowns

225
00:15:11,229 --> 00:15:13,687
who'd fill the river valleys with blood.

226
00:15:13,771 --> 00:15:14,604
Hm.

227
00:15:15,437 --> 00:15:16,437
Doesn't rhyme.

228
00:15:17,437 --> 00:15:18,812
All good predictions rhyme.

229
00:15:19,396 --> 00:15:22,771
I studied the girls born
around the Black Sun,

230
00:15:22,854 --> 00:15:26,562
and I found horrendous
internal mutations among them.

231
00:15:27,771 --> 00:15:29,021
I tried to cure them,

232
00:15:29,646 --> 00:15:31,562
locked them in towers for safekeeping,

233
00:15:31,646 --> 00:15:34,062
but the girls always died.

234
00:15:34,146 --> 00:15:36,604
Internal mutations?

235
00:15:37,146 --> 00:15:40,604
They were autopsied, of course,
to confirm my suspicions.

236
00:15:41,562 --> 00:15:44,729
But eliminating these women was
the lesser evil.

237
00:15:46,021 --> 00:15:48,354
They could've drowned entire kingdoms
in blood.

238
00:15:49,021 --> 00:15:52,271
If you'd been alive during
Falka's Rebellion, seen what I saw--

239
00:15:52,354 --> 00:15:54,062
Innocent women are dead.

240
00:15:58,854 --> 00:15:59,937
Hm.

241
00:16:00,396 --> 00:16:02,854
But not Renfri, the beautiful one.

242
00:16:04,812 --> 00:16:06,562
She's after you.

243
00:16:06,646 --> 00:16:08,729
Daughter of King Fredefalk of Creyden.

244
00:16:09,812 --> 00:16:12,896
I delivered the princess myself
in the middle of the afternoon

245
00:16:12,979 --> 00:16:13,979
in pitch black.

246
00:16:14,062 --> 00:16:17,104
Under the Black Sun, so... she's cursed.

247
00:16:17,187 --> 00:16:18,937
Do you consider me a fool, Witcher?

248
00:16:19,562 --> 00:16:23,354
Do you think I did not conduct research?
Renfri was acutely affected.

249
00:16:23,437 --> 00:16:27,271
Her stepmother, Aridea,
told me she tortured a canary,

250
00:16:27,354 --> 00:16:28,604
strangled two puppies,

251
00:16:28,687 --> 00:16:31,479
even gouged out her maid's eye
with a comb.

252
00:16:32,646 --> 00:16:35,312
I admit what happened next was not ideal,
but...

253
00:16:36,229 --> 00:16:39,604
with the lives of Aridea's own children
on the line, we had to act.

254
00:16:40,437 --> 00:16:44,354
So I dispatched someone
to follow Renfri into the woods.

255
00:16:44,437 --> 00:16:45,937
We found him in the brush,

256
00:16:46,021 --> 00:16:48,729
Renfri's antique brooch
jammed into his ear.

257
00:16:51,062 --> 00:16:55,187
After that, I organized a manhunt
to find the princess, but... eh...

258
00:16:55,854 --> 00:16:56,812
she was gone.

259
00:16:58,104 --> 00:16:59,104
Two years.

260
00:17:00,021 --> 00:17:01,562
Until she reappeared,

261
00:17:01,646 --> 00:17:04,479
robbing and murdering merchants
on the roads of Mahakam.

262
00:17:04,562 --> 00:17:06,979
Impaled them on sticks at first,
but soon,

263
00:17:07,979 --> 00:17:09,479
she picked up sword skills.

264
00:17:10,771 --> 00:17:13,271
And now no man can defy her, it's said.

265
00:17:13,354 --> 00:17:15,896
You're not a man. You're a magician.

266
00:17:15,979 --> 00:17:18,937
-She's resistant to magic.
-That's impossible in humans.

267
00:17:19,771 --> 00:17:20,646
Not...

268
00:17:21,896 --> 00:17:23,021
mutated ones.

269
00:17:24,146 --> 00:17:26,396
She's chased me for years,
bent on revenge.

270
00:17:26,479 --> 00:17:29,937
And now she's tracked me here,
just as you arrived.

271
00:17:31,812 --> 00:17:32,646
Destiny.

272
00:17:35,729 --> 00:17:36,812
Kill her.

273
00:17:38,812 --> 00:17:40,104
I'll pay you anything.

274
00:17:40,187 --> 00:17:41,646
I kill monsters.

275
00:17:41,729 --> 00:17:45,146
The kikimora kills because it's hungry,
Renfri kills for pleasure.

276
00:17:45,229 --> 00:17:48,312
She is a monster.
She is the last of Lilit's women.

277
00:17:49,146 --> 00:17:51,854
And she possesses the power
to destroy us all.

278
00:17:52,562 --> 00:17:55,229
I don't believe anyone has that power.

279
00:17:59,729 --> 00:18:03,729
With the fate of the Continent at stake,
is that a chance you're willing to take?

280
00:18:05,021 --> 00:18:06,021
There's your rhyme.

281
00:18:09,729 --> 00:18:11,437
Killing Renfri is...

282
00:18:11,937 --> 00:18:13,437
the lesser evil.

283
00:18:14,896 --> 00:18:16,437
Evil is evil, Stregobor.

284
00:18:17,229 --> 00:18:19,312
Lesser, greater,

285
00:18:20,187 --> 00:18:21,187
middling...

286
00:18:22,187 --> 00:18:23,187
it's all the same.

287
00:18:24,396 --> 00:18:25,812
I'm not judging you.

288
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:28,104
I haven't only done good
in my life either.

289
00:18:30,021 --> 00:18:31,021
But now,

290
00:18:31,979 --> 00:18:35,354
if I have to choose
between one evil and another,

291
00:18:37,687 --> 00:18:39,437
then I prefer not to choose at all.

292
00:18:49,229 --> 00:18:51,229
-[laughter]
-[folk music playing]

293
00:18:59,437 --> 00:19:03,187
These shindigs need a touch
of the old abracadabra.

294
00:19:04,354 --> 00:19:06,021
At your service, Your Majesty.

295
00:19:06,104 --> 00:19:08,104
Tricks and illusions to delight.

296
00:19:08,604 --> 00:19:11,771
He means to pull a disappearing act.
don't you?

297
00:19:12,479 --> 00:19:13,896
-No.
-Hm.

298
00:19:23,646 --> 00:19:26,562
I saw the Wraiths of MÃ¶rhogg
over the channel this morning.

299
00:19:26,646 --> 00:19:28,312
Yes, you mentioned.

300
00:19:28,396 --> 00:19:29,896
-Who?
-No good will come of it.

301
00:19:29,979 --> 00:19:31,604
They're an omen of war.

302
00:19:31,687 --> 00:19:34,146
The North has been at war
since Nilfgaard took Ebbing.

303
00:19:34,604 --> 00:19:38,396
If legend is true,
the Wild Hunt's years behind the curve.

304
00:19:38,812 --> 00:19:41,604
The Nilfgaardian force
crossed the Amell Pass.

305
00:19:41,687 --> 00:19:43,521
Headed to Sodden, if they're smart.

306
00:19:43,604 --> 00:19:47,312
And if not, 50 of your Skelligen ships
are on the way.

307
00:19:47,396 --> 00:19:50,021
We have more knights.
We are prepared in case--

308
00:19:50,104 --> 00:19:51,187
Prepared for what?

309
00:19:54,354 --> 00:19:56,312
Nothing for you to be concerned about.

310
00:19:57,062 --> 00:19:58,937
Your dismissive tone says it is.

311
00:19:59,021 --> 00:20:00,854
We're talking of war, girl.

312
00:20:01,854 --> 00:20:02,896
With Nilfgaard?

313
00:20:04,437 --> 00:20:05,437
-Why?
-Eist!

314
00:20:05,521 --> 00:20:08,604
Should we fall to Nilfgaard,
your granddaughter will rule.

315
00:20:09,354 --> 00:20:11,062
She needs to understand the way of things.

316
00:20:11,146 --> 00:20:14,146
We will not fall,
because we are not under attack!

317
00:20:15,479 --> 00:20:16,812
She's a child.

318
00:20:17,687 --> 00:20:20,646
You won your first battle in Hochebuz
when you were my age.

319
00:20:21,396 --> 00:20:22,604
I've heard the ballad.

320
00:20:22,687 --> 00:20:24,729
Pretty ballads hide bastard truths.

321
00:20:26,521 --> 00:20:27,604
It's a catchy song.

322
00:20:27,687 --> 00:20:29,437
Three thousand of my men died.

323
00:20:33,396 --> 00:20:34,771
If we must do this now,

324
00:20:35,396 --> 00:20:36,729
here is your first lesson.

325
00:20:38,854 --> 00:20:43,146
As in life, it is impossible always
to be fully prepared for battle.

326
00:20:44,479 --> 00:20:46,229
Keep your sword close...

327
00:20:47,062 --> 00:20:48,312
and keep moving.

328
00:20:49,187 --> 00:20:50,812
-[song ends]
-[cheering]

329
00:20:50,896 --> 00:20:53,021
Your Majesty... Your Majesty.

330
00:20:53,646 --> 00:20:56,562
Thank you for allowing our company
at this splendid affair.

331
00:20:57,187 --> 00:20:59,396
Your Majesties. Your Highness.

332
00:21:02,437 --> 00:21:03,937
Would you honor me with a dance?

333
00:21:05,479 --> 00:21:07,312
Uh... Martin--

334
00:21:07,396 --> 00:21:08,562
She'd love to.

335
00:21:36,562 --> 00:21:39,812
Reminds me
of your daughter's betrothal feast.

336
00:21:41,646 --> 00:21:45,187
The night you finally saw sense, said yes.

337
00:21:46,146 --> 00:21:48,396
Made me the happiest man
on the Continent.

338
00:21:49,729 --> 00:21:51,646
I did it to save my kingdom.

339
00:21:52,812 --> 00:21:53,646
And, no,

340
00:21:54,479 --> 00:21:56,687
you may not leave this shindig.

341
00:22:05,604 --> 00:22:07,646
[whispers]
Your Majesty, my scouts have returned.

342
00:22:09,437 --> 00:22:11,437
Nilfgaard is on its way to Cintra.

343
00:22:18,521 --> 00:22:19,896
[Queen] I stand corrected.

344
00:22:24,312 --> 00:22:25,312
They're here.

345
00:22:29,187 --> 00:22:30,604
They're already here.

346
00:22:36,646 --> 00:22:38,312
So much for being smart.

347
00:22:40,562 --> 00:22:41,937
You should tell the girl.

348
00:22:44,854 --> 00:22:47,021
[Queen] Let her enjoy this night in peace.

349
00:22:48,937 --> 00:22:50,729
It may be her last for a while.

350
00:22:58,021 --> 00:23:00,021
[cheering]

351
00:23:04,437 --> 00:23:06,104
[Roach neighing]

352
00:23:08,896 --> 00:23:10,979
[birdsong]

353
00:23:17,229 --> 00:23:18,896
[twigs cracking]

354
00:23:36,354 --> 00:23:37,604
The girl this morning,

355
00:23:38,979 --> 00:23:40,729
she took you to see Stregobor,
didn't she?

356
00:23:46,354 --> 00:23:49,312
I know who you are, Renfri.

357
00:23:51,354 --> 00:23:53,562
You know that I want
to kill Stregobor, then.

358
00:23:55,896 --> 00:23:58,937
I used to be a princess.
Did he tell you that?

359
00:24:01,562 --> 00:24:04,187
Until he sent a thug into the woods
to kill me.

360
00:24:04,271 --> 00:24:05,396
You killed him.

361
00:24:06,021 --> 00:24:07,312
With my mother's brooch.

362
00:24:19,812 --> 00:24:20,937
[sighs]

363
00:24:32,604 --> 00:24:34,521
Stregobor's man raped me...

364
00:24:37,229 --> 00:24:38,771
robbed me and let me go.

365
00:24:41,979 --> 00:24:43,271
No more princess.

366
00:24:47,271 --> 00:24:48,437
I had to survive.

367
00:24:50,312 --> 00:24:52,687
I stole rather than starve.

368
00:24:53,729 --> 00:24:55,437
I killed rather than be killed.

369
00:24:59,104 --> 00:25:00,854
Nohorn and the others saved me.

370
00:25:02,854 --> 00:25:06,146
And they'll be by my side at the market
as I get my revenge.

371
00:25:06,229 --> 00:25:09,437
Lilit help me,
I will take down anyone in my way.

372
00:25:14,104 --> 00:25:15,146
Unless...

373
00:25:16,437 --> 00:25:17,937
destiny intervenes.

374
00:25:25,812 --> 00:25:27,812
You want me to kill Stregobor for you.

375
00:25:29,479 --> 00:25:30,812
It's the lesser evil.

376
00:25:31,479 --> 00:25:33,104
So I keep getting told.

377
00:25:41,437 --> 00:25:43,187
Stregobor asked you to kill me too.

378
00:25:44,979 --> 00:25:47,396
'Cause I was a girl born
during an eclipse?

379
00:25:49,146 --> 00:25:51,312
I could've become so many things.

380
00:25:52,604 --> 00:25:54,062
Queen Calanthe of Cintra,

381
00:25:54,604 --> 00:25:56,729
she just won her first battle at Hochebuz.

382
00:25:58,021 --> 00:26:00,729
But here I am trying
to convince you I'm not--

383
00:26:00,812 --> 00:26:01,812
A monster.

384
00:26:05,021 --> 00:26:05,896
Are you?

385
00:26:08,229 --> 00:26:09,271
How am I to know?

386
00:26:09,979 --> 00:26:12,604
When I cut my finger, I bleed.
That's human, right?

387
00:26:13,396 --> 00:26:15,062
When I overeat, my stomach aches.

388
00:26:15,146 --> 00:26:16,896
When I'm happy, I laugh.

389
00:26:16,979 --> 00:26:19,562
When I'm upset, I swear.
And when I hate someone...

390
00:26:19,646 --> 00:26:21,896
for stealing my whole life from me,
I kill him.

391
00:26:23,021 --> 00:26:24,062
Hm.

392
00:26:25,354 --> 00:26:27,062
People call you a monster too.

393
00:26:27,729 --> 00:26:28,896
A mutant.

394
00:26:28,979 --> 00:26:30,396
What if they come after you?

395
00:26:31,271 --> 00:26:32,146
Attack you?

396
00:26:32,562 --> 00:26:33,562
They have.

397
00:26:35,521 --> 00:26:37,812
Why not kill them?

398
00:26:37,896 --> 00:26:38,729
Because then...

399
00:26:42,396 --> 00:26:44,312
I am what they say I am.

400
00:26:49,521 --> 00:26:51,146
If I tell you, Witcher,

401
00:26:52,146 --> 00:26:55,729
that I can neither forgive Stregobor
nor renounce my revenge,

402
00:26:56,937 --> 00:26:57,937
is that it?

403
00:26:59,521 --> 00:27:00,896
I admit I'm a monster?

404
00:27:01,979 --> 00:27:02,854
Yes.

405
00:27:04,229 --> 00:27:05,062
Or...

406
00:27:05,729 --> 00:27:07,271
you can leave Blaviken...

407
00:27:08,604 --> 00:27:09,979
and finally live.

408
00:27:15,479 --> 00:27:16,812
You choose, Princess.

409
00:27:24,229 --> 00:27:25,396
[Roach snorts]

410
00:27:36,312 --> 00:27:38,021
[wind whistling]

411
00:27:41,146 --> 00:27:42,687
[neighing]

412
00:27:44,271 --> 00:27:46,271
[man yells] Keep it steady!

413
00:27:54,604 --> 00:27:55,562
[man yells] Steady!

414
00:27:56,146 --> 00:27:57,312
[snorts]

415
00:27:57,437 --> 00:27:59,562
[man yells] Stand by!

416
00:28:12,562 --> 00:28:14,229
[neighing uneasily]

417
00:28:16,646 --> 00:28:18,646
[thunder of hooves]

418
00:28:27,771 --> 00:28:29,771
[all yelling]

419
00:28:35,062 --> 00:28:36,771
[man yells] Hold...

420
00:28:36,854 --> 00:28:40,979
[Calanthe] Charge!

421
00:28:57,062 --> 00:28:59,104
Not fair that I'm trapped here.

422
00:28:59,187 --> 00:29:01,521
I could magically put you to sleep,
Princess.

423
00:29:03,687 --> 00:29:04,771
Just an idea.

424
00:29:04,854 --> 00:29:07,687
-It's been two days.
-For you and everyone else in the castle.

425
00:29:07,771 --> 00:29:10,104
The King and Queen ordered us
to remain here,

426
00:29:11,937 --> 00:29:13,396
and that's what we shall do.

427
00:29:16,646 --> 00:29:17,979
And why are you not there?

428
00:29:19,146 --> 00:29:20,354
Wherever they are.

429
00:29:21,354 --> 00:29:22,687
My duty is to protect you.

430
00:29:22,771 --> 00:29:24,437
You're resentful of that burden.

431
00:29:24,521 --> 00:29:25,937
It's the greatest honor of my life.

432
00:29:28,021 --> 00:29:30,437
[scoffs] You are both incredibly boring.

433
00:29:34,896 --> 00:29:35,854
[sighs]

434
00:29:40,104 --> 00:29:41,562
Many, many years ago,

435
00:29:41,646 --> 00:29:44,812
sorcerers were known
to lock little girls in towers.

436
00:29:45,562 --> 00:29:47,271
I'm beginning to understand why.

437
00:29:47,354 --> 00:29:49,562
You know cautionary tales don't work
on me.

438
00:29:50,479 --> 00:29:52,146
The girls were said to be cursed.

439
00:29:52,229 --> 00:29:54,771
They were said to announce
the end of the human race.

440
00:29:54,854 --> 00:29:55,812
Ooh.

441
00:29:57,062 --> 00:30:00,021
So they were systematically killed.

442
00:30:00,104 --> 00:30:01,104
The end.

443
00:30:03,687 --> 00:30:04,812
[sighs]

444
00:30:13,687 --> 00:30:14,896
[man sighs]

445
00:30:21,312 --> 00:30:22,771
Will my grandmother be all right?

446
00:30:25,062 --> 00:30:25,937
[sighs]

447
00:30:33,354 --> 00:30:35,354
You will be all right, Princess.

448
00:30:36,354 --> 00:30:37,854
You are her blood.

449
00:30:40,896 --> 00:30:43,354
And the apple never falls far
from the tree.

450
00:30:55,271 --> 00:30:56,771
[yelling]

451
00:31:01,896 --> 00:31:02,896
[yells]

452
00:31:06,146 --> 00:31:07,229
[groans]

453
00:31:10,771 --> 00:31:11,854
We're losing!

454
00:31:19,229 --> 00:31:21,687
[screams] The ships from Skellige?

455
00:31:21,771 --> 00:31:23,646
There's been a storm, Your Majesty.

456
00:31:25,146 --> 00:31:26,062
No one's coming!

457
00:31:26,146 --> 00:31:27,021
[yells]

458
00:31:27,104 --> 00:31:30,187
Then we fight alone.
We cannot surrender Cintra!

459
00:31:30,271 --> 00:31:31,271
Nor will we!

460
00:31:39,396 --> 00:31:40,521
[gasps]

461
00:31:43,979 --> 00:31:45,521
[gasping]

462
00:31:46,312 --> 00:31:47,271
Eist!

463
00:31:54,437 --> 00:31:56,437
[wails]

464
00:31:59,062 --> 00:32:01,062
[screams]

465
00:32:02,562 --> 00:32:03,396
[gasps]

466
00:32:06,396 --> 00:32:07,562
Move!

467
00:32:07,646 --> 00:32:08,521
[gasps]

468
00:32:10,937 --> 00:32:12,479
No!

469
00:32:15,729 --> 00:32:20,187
[woman] Guide us to the safety
of your arms, hold us in your light,

470
00:32:20,687 --> 00:32:24,729
protect us from the imperial darkness
that threatens our souls.

471
00:32:27,479 --> 00:32:28,687
[gasps]

472
00:32:30,604 --> 00:32:31,771
Princess Cirilla...

473
00:32:32,437 --> 00:32:33,479
Hm.

474
00:32:37,646 --> 00:32:39,271
-[sighs]
-[Martin] Are we going to be okay?

475
00:32:39,354 --> 00:32:42,729
[woman] Don't worry, Martin.
The Queen will defeat Nilfgaard.

476
00:32:43,646 --> 00:32:44,896
We will go home soon.

477
00:32:51,896 --> 00:32:53,062
Your Highness.

478
00:32:55,396 --> 00:32:56,604
[door opens]

479
00:32:56,687 --> 00:32:58,771
[man] ...won't stop
until they get what they want!

480
00:32:58,854 --> 00:33:01,271
[Calanthe] ...a hundred arrows
on my body first! [sobbing]

481
00:33:01,354 --> 00:33:03,146
Your Majesty, what must...

482
00:33:03,229 --> 00:33:04,146
[door slams]

483
00:33:08,354 --> 00:33:09,604
[gasping]

484
00:33:22,062 --> 00:33:23,479
My sweet child.

485
00:33:28,104 --> 00:33:29,104
Careful.

486
00:33:31,104 --> 00:33:32,062
Careful.

487
00:33:37,354 --> 00:33:39,437
-[sobs]
-Cintra is under attack.

488
00:33:44,062 --> 00:33:45,271
Eist is dead.

489
00:33:52,771 --> 00:33:55,146
Nilfgaard have made their way
into the city.

490
00:33:55,812 --> 00:33:56,896
Why?

491
00:34:00,021 --> 00:34:01,187
The citizens...

492
00:34:01,937 --> 00:34:04,396
how many of them are safe
within our walls?

493
00:34:04,771 --> 00:34:07,979
A hundred or so, Your Majesty.
The guests from the banquet.

494
00:34:10,271 --> 00:34:11,396
The supplies...

495
00:34:12,521 --> 00:34:13,812
check we have enough.

496
00:34:16,771 --> 00:34:17,604
Aye.

497
00:34:26,062 --> 00:34:27,771
You've been brave, my child,

498
00:34:29,396 --> 00:34:30,521
while I've been gone?

499
00:34:30,604 --> 00:34:32,729
I haven't. Ask Mousesack.
I've been impatient.

500
00:34:32,812 --> 00:34:35,354
You will rule this land someday.

501
00:34:36,646 --> 00:34:38,771
You know that, don't you?

502
00:34:39,521 --> 00:34:41,062
[breathing heavily]

503
00:34:41,854 --> 00:34:43,396
Why are you saying all this?

504
00:34:47,479 --> 00:34:48,729
Are you dying?

505
00:34:51,479 --> 00:34:52,646
My sweet child,

506
00:34:55,146 --> 00:34:58,479
when I go,
it will be far more dramatic than this.

507
00:34:59,396 --> 00:35:00,437
[chuckles]

508
00:35:12,937 --> 00:35:14,146
Now, child...

509
00:35:18,146 --> 00:35:19,354
let me rest.

510
00:35:19,979 --> 00:35:21,062
Hm?

511
00:35:23,354 --> 00:35:24,521
[sighs]

512
00:35:44,104 --> 00:35:46,104
[rumble of battle]

513
00:35:48,354 --> 00:35:50,354
[crowd clamoring]

514
00:35:53,771 --> 00:35:55,354
[Mousesack] They've reached the gate.

515
00:36:01,979 --> 00:36:03,521
[whirring]

516
00:36:03,604 --> 00:36:05,646
[whooshing]

517
00:36:08,979 --> 00:36:10,021
[Ciri] What are you doing?

518
00:36:13,354 --> 00:36:14,521
[yelling]

519
00:36:20,271 --> 00:36:21,521
How long will it hold?

520
00:36:23,271 --> 00:36:24,937
As long as I hold.

521
00:36:26,396 --> 00:36:27,812
[gasping]

522
00:36:35,271 --> 00:36:36,146
[sighs]

523
00:36:36,229 --> 00:36:37,271
[birdsong]

524
00:36:37,354 --> 00:36:39,479
[Geralt] You know what Vesemir would say.

525
00:36:39,937 --> 00:36:42,854
"Witchers shouldn't play
at being white knights.

526
00:36:42,937 --> 00:36:45,146
We shouldn't try and uphold the law.

527
00:36:46,771 --> 00:36:48,187
We don't show off.

528
00:36:48,687 --> 00:36:50,437
We get paid in coin."

529
00:36:52,854 --> 00:36:53,729
And he's right.

530
00:36:55,354 --> 00:36:57,187
[blows]

531
00:36:57,729 --> 00:36:58,687
Hm.

532
00:36:59,479 --> 00:37:01,312
Want to hear about my first monster?

533
00:37:01,896 --> 00:37:03,146
[snorts]

534
00:37:03,229 --> 00:37:05,354
Wasn't 50 miles outside of Kaer Morhen.

535
00:37:07,312 --> 00:37:08,521
He was huge.

536
00:37:09,396 --> 00:37:11,271
-Stinking.
-[nickers]

537
00:37:11,354 --> 00:37:12,854
-Bald head.
-[snorts]

538
00:37:12,937 --> 00:37:14,104
-Rotten teeth.
-[blows]

539
00:37:16,812 --> 00:37:18,646
He pulled that girl from the cart,

540
00:37:19,479 --> 00:37:22,104
tore her dress off
in front of her father and said,

541
00:37:22,896 --> 00:37:24,479
"It's time you met a real man."

542
00:37:26,687 --> 00:37:28,521
I told him it was time he met one too.

543
00:37:31,646 --> 00:37:33,312
It took two strikes to kill him.

544
00:37:34,854 --> 00:37:35,896
They weren't clean.

545
00:37:36,937 --> 00:37:38,396
But they were spectacular.

546
00:37:40,646 --> 00:37:42,604
I turned to that girl afterwards.

547
00:37:42,687 --> 00:37:44,521
She was drenched in the man's blood.

548
00:37:46,354 --> 00:37:47,604
She took one look at me,

549
00:37:48,479 --> 00:37:50,604
screamed, vomited,

550
00:37:51,354 --> 00:37:52,437
and passed out.

551
00:37:53,479 --> 00:37:54,896
[snorts]

552
00:37:54,979 --> 00:37:55,812
Yeah.

553
00:37:57,396 --> 00:37:59,521
-I thought the world needed me too.
-[nickering]

554
00:38:03,854 --> 00:38:05,562
[Renfri] Who were you talking to?

555
00:38:06,479 --> 00:38:07,562
[sighs]

556
00:38:11,354 --> 00:38:12,479
I talk to my horse.

557
00:38:14,229 --> 00:38:15,937
-That's sad.
-Is it?

558
00:38:20,354 --> 00:38:21,437
Tell me, Witcher.

559
00:38:22,937 --> 00:38:24,521
You don't believe in destiny

560
00:38:25,062 --> 00:38:26,271
or the lesser evil.

561
00:38:28,229 --> 00:38:29,437
What do you believe in?

562
00:38:29,521 --> 00:38:30,521
You mean...

563
00:38:31,146 --> 00:38:32,562
who do I believe.

564
00:38:33,104 --> 00:38:34,271
I don't pick sides.

565
00:38:34,687 --> 00:38:35,979
You just kill monsters.

566
00:39:02,187 --> 00:39:03,437
I've made my decision.

567
00:39:05,812 --> 00:39:09,187
You gave me an ultimatum
and I find they work.

568
00:39:12,146 --> 00:39:13,479
Tomorrow, I'll leave Blaviken.

569
00:39:14,896 --> 00:39:15,896
For good.

570
00:39:24,062 --> 00:39:25,646
My men, they love me
and I love them.

571
00:39:27,021 --> 00:39:30,062
But it's been a long time
since someone saw me.

572
00:39:35,646 --> 00:39:36,771
When I was a girl,

573
00:39:38,062 --> 00:39:40,479
my mother used to run her fingers...

574
00:39:41,062 --> 00:39:42,521
over my forehead.

575
00:39:44,562 --> 00:39:45,937
She'd say...

576
00:39:46,646 --> 00:39:48,854
she'd give a lovely lintar...

577
00:39:50,146 --> 00:39:52,979
to know the thoughts
going around in there.

578
00:40:43,437 --> 00:40:45,646
[soldier] Fire at will! Fire!

579
00:40:45,729 --> 00:40:47,396
Bring more fire!

580
00:41:02,896 --> 00:41:04,187
[cheering]

581
00:41:11,479 --> 00:41:14,937
Your Majesty, the Nilfgaardians
will breach the castle gates.

582
00:41:15,021 --> 00:41:16,021
[Mousesack] Have breached.

583
00:41:17,437 --> 00:41:19,979
My powers could not hold them any longer,
Your Majesty.

584
00:41:20,062 --> 00:41:21,771
Now what? What do we do?

585
00:41:22,354 --> 00:41:23,187
[Calanthe] Mousesack.

586
00:41:24,937 --> 00:41:26,812
[breathing heavily]

587
00:41:27,937 --> 00:41:29,812
[whispers] He's in the gatekeep.

588
00:41:31,896 --> 00:41:34,979
Destiny may yet side with us.

589
00:41:41,771 --> 00:41:42,604
Danek.

590
00:41:46,562 --> 00:41:47,562
It's time.

591
00:41:47,646 --> 00:41:49,687
[army outside howling]

592
00:41:50,146 --> 00:41:51,271
What?

593
00:41:53,646 --> 00:41:55,021
Wait, where are you going?

594
00:41:59,937 --> 00:42:01,146
[Calanthe] Come here, child.

595
00:42:14,646 --> 00:42:16,271
The gates are down!

596
00:42:17,896 --> 00:42:19,146
Lesson number two.

597
00:42:21,521 --> 00:42:24,229
Know when it's time to stop moving.

598
00:42:25,521 --> 00:42:26,521
You're conceding.

599
00:42:28,104 --> 00:42:30,021
Nilfgaard takes no prisoners.

600
00:42:31,646 --> 00:42:35,271
Which means that right now,
my citizens are being tortured.

601
00:42:36,646 --> 00:42:37,854
[screams]

602
00:42:38,979 --> 00:42:43,437
Their insides are being pulled
to their outsides while they watch.

603
00:42:46,521 --> 00:42:48,437
Their legs lit on fire.

604
00:42:49,062 --> 00:42:51,521
Their tongues fed to the dogs.

605
00:42:55,979 --> 00:42:56,979
Your Majesty.

606
00:42:57,437 --> 00:42:58,687
-He's gone.
-What?

607
00:43:02,979 --> 00:43:04,854
In the face of the inevitable, Cirilla,

608
00:43:06,354 --> 00:43:09,604
good leaders should always choose mercy.

609
00:43:11,021 --> 00:43:13,604
In the future,
you will be wise to do the same.

610
00:43:16,104 --> 00:43:17,021
Lazlo,

611
00:43:18,021 --> 00:43:18,937
bring her cloak.

612
00:43:20,437 --> 00:43:21,729
What? No.

613
00:43:22,437 --> 00:43:24,479
Continue to be brave. Promise me.

614
00:43:25,229 --> 00:43:27,062
You are the Lion Cub of Cintra.

615
00:43:27,812 --> 00:43:30,812
-You are destined for great things.
-I can't do this without you.

616
00:43:30,896 --> 00:43:31,979
We must go, Your Highness.

617
00:43:32,062 --> 00:43:34,521
-[screams] No!
-[roaring]

618
00:43:37,521 --> 00:43:38,604
[sighs]

619
00:43:41,812 --> 00:43:42,729
Go.

620
00:43:44,396 --> 00:43:45,687
The world depends on it.

621
00:43:47,146 --> 00:43:48,854
[battle raging outside]

622
00:43:58,187 --> 00:43:59,312
I love you.

623
00:44:05,229 --> 00:44:07,521
Find Geralt of Rivia.

624
00:44:09,354 --> 00:44:10,854
He is your destiny.

625
00:44:28,437 --> 00:44:29,562
[sobs]

626
00:44:37,854 --> 00:44:38,729
Your Majesty.

627
00:44:38,812 --> 00:44:39,812
I saw it too.

628
00:44:42,771 --> 00:44:44,146
It is why they came.

629
00:44:45,271 --> 00:44:46,437
I will deliver her.

630
00:44:49,021 --> 00:44:50,521
I give you my word.

631
00:44:50,604 --> 00:44:51,771
[gasping]

632
00:44:57,979 --> 00:44:58,854
Mousesack.

633
00:45:02,187 --> 00:45:03,396
Your service...

634
00:45:04,396 --> 00:45:06,604
has been an honor to us all.

635
00:45:08,687 --> 00:45:09,854
As has yours.

636
00:45:13,146 --> 00:45:14,521
Your Majesty.

637
00:45:33,146 --> 00:45:35,521
I'm sorry to disturb, my lady.
It is time.

638
00:45:36,229 --> 00:45:37,271
Nilfgaard is nigh.

639
00:45:51,729 --> 00:45:52,729
It is time.

640
00:46:05,312 --> 00:46:06,812
[locks door]

641
00:46:19,062 --> 00:46:20,146
We can leave.

642
00:46:21,521 --> 00:46:23,062
We can find a way out.

643
00:46:24,646 --> 00:46:25,604
This...

644
00:46:27,521 --> 00:46:28,854
This is our way out.

645
00:47:09,812 --> 00:47:11,271
-What are you doing?
-It's me, my son.

646
00:47:11,354 --> 00:47:13,354
-What is this?
-It's okay.

647
00:47:14,021 --> 00:47:14,854
[whispers]

648
00:48:29,354 --> 00:48:30,437
Horses.

649
00:48:31,937 --> 00:48:32,937
Princess, come.

650
00:48:34,104 --> 00:48:34,937
Hey!

651
00:48:36,896 --> 00:48:38,521
-Keep going.
-No!

652
00:48:39,521 --> 00:48:42,146
Princess, I gave your grandmother my word.

653
00:48:42,854 --> 00:48:44,062
Allow me to keep it.

654
00:48:45,229 --> 00:48:46,062
Go.

655
00:48:47,937 --> 00:48:49,729
My grandmother said I had to leave.

656
00:48:49,812 --> 00:48:51,979
Why? Why is Nilfgaard here?

657
00:48:52,062 --> 00:48:54,562
-Why does the world depend on it?
-Hold on, Your Highness.

658
00:49:00,521 --> 00:49:01,854
-[neighs]
-Hyah!

659
00:49:07,521 --> 00:49:08,896
[snorting]

660
00:49:09,729 --> 00:49:11,437
[Lazlo] We're getting close to the gate.

661
00:49:13,062 --> 00:49:15,104
I've been protected my whole life,
Lazlo.

662
00:49:15,187 --> 00:49:16,104
Why?

663
00:49:22,562 --> 00:49:24,437
-[Ciri screams]
-[neighs]

664
00:49:59,687 --> 00:50:02,437
[Renfri] You were in the market.
Covered in blood.

665
00:50:05,604 --> 00:50:07,854
[echoing] You say you can't choose,
but you had to.

666
00:50:08,312 --> 00:50:10,271
And you'll never know
if you were right.

667
00:50:15,396 --> 00:50:17,021
Your reward will be a stoning.

668
00:50:18,354 --> 00:50:19,646
And you will run.

669
00:50:20,396 --> 00:50:23,354
You will try to outrun the girl
in the woods, but you cannot.

670
00:50:24,104 --> 00:50:25,604
-She is your destiny.
-Renfri!

671
00:50:35,937 --> 00:50:37,021
The market.

672
00:50:38,146 --> 00:50:39,396
[bleating]

673
00:50:49,812 --> 00:50:50,979
She knew you'd come.

674
00:50:53,771 --> 00:50:55,104
Where's Renfri?

675
00:50:55,187 --> 00:50:57,437
She's at the tower
with your little friend,

676
00:50:58,229 --> 00:50:59,187
Marilka.

677
00:50:59,771 --> 00:51:01,979
She gave us a message
to pass on to you.

678
00:51:02,437 --> 00:51:04,187
You have to choose the lesser evil.

679
00:51:04,271 --> 00:51:05,687
It's an ultimatum.

680
00:51:05,812 --> 00:51:06,687
[draws sword]

681
00:51:06,771 --> 00:51:07,687
Get it?

682
00:51:11,021 --> 00:51:11,896
Fuck.

683
00:51:11,979 --> 00:51:13,104
Hm.

684
00:51:25,229 --> 00:51:27,229
[yelling]

685
00:51:30,937 --> 00:51:31,854
Witcher!

686
00:52:08,271 --> 00:52:09,104
[Marilka] Geralt!

687
00:52:09,729 --> 00:52:11,062
[screams] Geralt!

688
00:52:13,687 --> 00:52:14,521
[sobs] No!

689
00:52:16,896 --> 00:52:17,771
[sighs]

690
00:52:24,479 --> 00:52:26,521
-You chose.
-Let the girl go.

691
00:52:30,437 --> 00:52:31,562
I will kill her.

692
00:52:33,687 --> 00:52:36,729
I will kill everyone here
until Stregobor comes down.

693
00:52:37,937 --> 00:52:38,979
Leave Blaviken.

694
00:52:40,729 --> 00:52:41,854
It's not too late.

695
00:52:42,687 --> 00:52:44,021
Magic doesn't work on me.

696
00:52:45,646 --> 00:52:46,937
Silver does, though.

697
00:52:47,021 --> 00:52:48,354
Silver is for monsters.

698
00:52:48,437 --> 00:52:49,354
-[grunts]
-[screams]

699
00:52:52,396 --> 00:52:55,021
-If we cross swords...
-I won't be able to stop.

700
00:53:07,271 --> 00:53:09,604
They created me just as they created you.

701
00:53:10,021 --> 00:53:11,479
We're not so different.

702
00:53:13,521 --> 00:53:15,062
[groans]

703
00:54:28,062 --> 00:54:30,979
The girl in the woods will be
with you always.

704
00:54:32,771 --> 00:54:34,021
She is your destiny.

705
00:55:10,896 --> 00:55:12,896
[screams]

706
00:55:16,521 --> 00:55:18,521
Get-- get back here, you little--

707
00:55:19,104 --> 00:55:20,312
-[screams]
-[yells in pain]

708
00:55:21,521 --> 00:55:23,396
[rumbling]

709
00:55:23,854 --> 00:55:25,812
-[screams]
-[yells in pain]

710
00:55:26,437 --> 00:55:28,687
[rumbling]

711
00:55:28,771 --> 00:55:31,062
[screaming]

712
00:55:40,521 --> 00:55:41,854
[gasping]

713
00:55:48,271 --> 00:55:50,104
[gasping] No. No!

714
00:56:26,854 --> 00:56:28,062
Incredible.

715
00:56:30,396 --> 00:56:31,271
[sighs]

716
00:56:33,562 --> 00:56:34,396
Marilka.

717
00:56:35,729 --> 00:56:38,104
Marilka? Marilka!

718
00:56:38,937 --> 00:56:40,187
Get me a cart.

719
00:56:40,271 --> 00:56:42,479
We'll take her to the tower
for an autopsy.

720
00:56:44,521 --> 00:56:46,729
If you touch a single hair on her head...

721
00:56:47,604 --> 00:56:49,271
yours will be on the ground next.

722
00:56:49,354 --> 00:56:50,562
Have you gone mad?

723
00:56:51,479 --> 00:56:52,562
Her mutation,

724
00:56:53,479 --> 00:56:54,729
it influences people.

725
00:56:54,812 --> 00:56:56,937
That's how she got these men
to follow her.

726
00:56:57,354 --> 00:56:58,604
We need to take it.

727
00:57:02,687 --> 00:57:05,354
She got to you too, didn't she?

728
00:57:07,354 --> 00:57:08,354
Do not...

729
00:57:08,937 --> 00:57:10,062
touch her.

730
00:57:13,521 --> 00:57:14,562
Witcher.

731
00:57:16,146 --> 00:57:19,687
You butchered bodies
in the streets of Blaviken.

732
00:57:19,771 --> 00:57:21,979
-You're a beast!
-You endangered the girl.

733
00:57:22,062 --> 00:57:23,979
-[woman] Beast!
-[man] He's killed every single...

734
00:57:24,062 --> 00:57:27,437
-You took the law into your own hands.
-[woman] Bastard!

735
00:57:27,521 --> 00:57:29,437
-[crowd clamoring]
-[woman] He's a bad one!

736
00:57:29,521 --> 00:57:31,521
-[man] Get out of here!
-[man 2] Get out and don't...

737
00:57:31,604 --> 00:57:33,646
[woman] Go on! Butcher!

738
00:57:33,729 --> 00:57:35,312
You made a choice.

739
00:57:36,979 --> 00:57:39,604
And you'll never know
if it was the right one.

740
00:57:39,687 --> 00:57:41,354
-Die, Witcher!
-[clamoring]

741
00:57:44,604 --> 00:57:45,979
Die, Witcher!

742
00:57:57,021 --> 00:57:58,687
-Go, Witcher!
-Die!

743
00:58:01,396 --> 00:58:03,062
Get out of Blaviken, Geralt.

744
00:58:05,562 --> 00:58:06,771
Don't ever come back.

745
00:58:08,437 --> 00:58:09,646
Bastard!

746
00:58:15,604 --> 00:58:17,771
[yelling continues]

747
00:58:36,646 --> 00:58:39,354
[Renfri] The girl in the woods will be
with you always.

748
00:58:41,146 --> 00:58:42,479
She is your destiny.

